"4438","Statement: Government forces killed 244 civilians including 44 children, 30 ladies and 52 tortured to death during five-days of Geneva IIPeace conference","2014-01-27 11:52:00","Syria","Statement: Government forces killed 244 civilians including 44 children, 30 ladies and 52 tortured to death during five-days of Geneva IIPeace conference

The report only contains the Death toll of civilians during Geneva II Peace Conference 
 
Date of issue: 26/1/2014 
The Syrian Government did not show any sign of good gesture, especially with the most important matter: the lives of humans.
For the fifth-day of Geneva II peace conference bloodshed in Syria didn't stop, Government Forces continued committing shelling on residential buildings by missiles and dropping barrel bombs and Security forces continued torturing detainees in detention centers for a moment.

SNHR has documented within those three days of Geneva II conference the killing of 244 civilians, including 44 children, 30 women, and 52 victims have been tortured to death, the proportion of women and children is 30% of the victims, which is a very clear indication of the deliberate targeting of civilians. 
SNHR demand International Community to apply real pressure that forcing Syrian Government to cease immediately shelling and torture. 

