Statement Government forces killed 161 civilians including 22 children, 23 ladies and 36 tortured to death during the three-days of Peace conference 
Date of issue: 25/1/2014  
For the third-day of Geneva II peace conference bloodshed in Syria didn't stop, Government Forces continued committing shelling on residential buildings by missiles and dropping barrel bombs and Security forces continued torturing detainees in detention centers for a moment.
SNHR has documented within those three days of Geneva II conference the killing of 161 civilians, including 22 children, 23 women, and 36 victims have been tortured to death, the proportion of women and children is 31% of the victims, which is a very clear indication of the deliberate targeting of civilians. 
SNHR demand International Community to apply real pressure that forcing Syrian Government to cease immediately shelling and torture.  
