Surpassing 500 Days , Doctor &amp;amp; Activist Fares Hamdi Al-Zahoki is in detention
It has been 500 days now on the third arrest of Doctor and activist Fares
Hamdi Al-zahoki ,coming from his hometown Tsiel – Dar’a Province, a 50
year old, a husband and a father, was one of the prominent activists in
town who started the peaceful demonstration, as well as supplying medical
care to the wounded demonstrators within the modest capabilities available
in his hand.

His first detention was on 20.Aug.2011, when he was arrested by a
security’s patrol and taken to an unknown destination, where he was kept
for 5 days.

And later on same year, he was arrested again on 16.Sep, when a security’s
patrol stormed his house , crashed his car and took him with his son in to
custody, his arrest lasted till 05.Oct when he was released

His third and last arrest that lasted till the date that this statement
was published, took place on 24th of November same year, where he was
taken to an unknown destination, to be held as what is known as &quot; An
enforced disappearance &quot; status.

There is a serious concern on his fate, as there is no information on his
physical status up to the minute this statement was published, and he
hasn’t been charged with any offense yet, nor was his family allowed to
visit him
http://www.vdc-sy.info/index.php/en/details/detainees/39823

